# LPA UI Components & Design System

The app theme is DaisyUI 5 (`dim` theme) with Tailwind CSS 4, configured in `lightning-pose-app/web_ui/src/styles.css`.

## Styling & Component Library Guidelines

- **DaisyUI 5 First:** Always use DaisyUI component classes (`btn`, `input`, `select`, `range`, `badge`, `menu`, `tooltip`, `modal`, `card`, `alert`) before writing custom CSS.
  - Button sizes/variants: `btn btn-primary`, `btn btn-outline`, `btn btn-sm`, `btn btn-ghost`.
  - Badges & status: `badge badge-neutral`, `badge badge-success`, `badge badge-warning`, `badge badge-error`.
  - Dialogs: Use DaisyUI `<dialog class="modal">` with `<div class="modal-box">` and `<form method="dialog">` or Angular dialog components.
  - Tooltips: Use `tooltip` with `data-tip="..."` and positional modifiers (`tooltip-top`, `tooltip-bottom`).
- **Tailwind CSS 4 for Layout:** Use Tailwind utility classes for flexbox, grid, sizing, spacing, and layout (`flex`, `grid`, `gap-2`, `p-4`, `w-full`, `justify-between`).
- **Avoid Custom CSS Classes:** Avoid declaring one-off custom CSS classes in component `.css` files unless strictly necessary for canvas graphics, overlay coordinates, or tight pixel constraints.
- **Known LPA Exceptions:**
  - The Viewer frame and time fields stay custom (`.jump-field`) because DaisyUI `input` is too tall for that tight toolbar.
  - The seek slider uses DaisyUI `range`.

## Component Architecture & Placement

- **Reusable Presentational Widgets (`web_ui/src/app/components/`):**
  - Place a component here if it is reusable across multiple features or acts as a generic UI primitive (e.g. `path-bar`, `dropdown`, `dense-listbox`, `alert-dialog`).
  - Must be **purely presentational** (dumb): state in via `input()`, actions out via `output()`, two-way binding via `model()`.
  - **Never** inject domain backend services (`RpcService`, `ProjectInfoService`, `SessionService`) into reusable components.
  - **Required Collocation:** Each reusable component must have its `*.stories.ts` (Storybook) beside it. Add `*.spec.ts` only when the component encodes behavior worth guarding (see `.cursor/rules/lpa-web-ui-tests.mdc`); trivial presentational wrappers may rely on Storybook + parent/integration specs.
- **Feature-Specific UI:**
  - Keep domain-specific UI in its respective feature directory (e.g. `web_ui/src/app/viewer/`, `labeler/`, `video-player/`, `project-settings/`).
  - If a feature sub-widget is only used within that feature, keep it collocated within the feature folder rather than moving it to `components/`.
- **Anti-Pattern (Over-Componentization):**
  - Do NOT create an Angular component to wrap a simple DaisyUI element (e.g. do not create `<app-button>` to wrap `<button class="btn">`). Use native HTML with DaisyUI classes directly.

## Storybook Development

- **When to Add Stories:**
  - Mandatory for every component under `web_ui/src/app/components/`.
  - Encouraged for feature-level widgets when they can render in isolation with mock data.
- **Running Storybook:**
  - Storybook requires Node 26 on `PATH`:
    ```bash
    cd lightning-pose-app/web_ui && npm run storybook
    ```
    (Runs at http://localhost:6006).
- **Storybook vs Unit Tests:** Storybook is for visual inspection, state exploration, and interactive styling. It does NOT replace unit tests (`*.spec.ts`).
